    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Self-hosted n8n only:** this version uses the community node `n8n-nodes-ashdocs` (n8n verification pending), so it runs on self-hosted n8n. The HTTP version of the same template uses only built-in nodes and also runs on n8n Cloud.\n\n\n## Create and email invoices from new Google Sheets rows with ASHDOCS\n\nFreelancers, studios and small teams who already track billable work in a Google Sheet and want each finished row to become a real, numbered invoice without copying anything by hand.\n\n### How it works\n1. The **Google Sheets Trigger** checks the sheet every minute for new or changed rows.\n2. **Ready rows only** lets a row through when its Status is empty or `ready` and it has an email and a unit price. Rows already marked `sent` are skipped, so the workflow never invoices a row twice.\n3. ASHDOCS finds the customer by email, or creates them.\n4. **Create invoice** numbers the invoice and renders its PDF and payment page. An idempotency key built from the row means a retry returns the same invoice instead of a second one.\n5. **Send invoice** emails it to the client from ASHDOCS.\n6. The row is updated: Status `sent`, Invoice Number, Pay Link. If anything fails, Status becomes `error: …` with the reason, and the row waits for you to fix it and set Status back to `ready`.\n\n### Requirements\n- An ASHDOCS account (https://www.ashdocs.com/?utm_source=n8n&utm_medium=template&utm_campaign=sheets-to-invoice). Works on every ASHDOCS plan, including Free (100 credits a month).\n- A Google Sheets account\n- Self-hosted n8n with the community node `n8n-nodes-ashdocs` installed\n\n[ASHDOCS](https://www.ashdocs.com/?utm_source=n8n&utm_medium=template&utm_campaign=sheets-to-invoice) · [Docs](https://www.ashdocs.com/docs)",
        "height": 720,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "4b435d0e-c001-4d83-afe0-4daa944693bf",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1160,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup\n**Plan:** Works on every ASHDOCS plan, including Free (100 credits a month).\n\n1. Create an ASHDOCS account at https://www.ashdocs.com/?utm_source=n8n&utm_medium=template&utm_campaign=sheets-to-invoice and create an API key on the **API Keys** page of the dashboard. A test key makes watermarked test invoices while you try the workflow.\n2. Install the ASHDOCS community node: **Settings → Community nodes → Install**, enter `n8n-nodes-ashdocs`. Then open any ASHDOCS node and create the **ASHDOCS API** credential with your key.\n3. Create a sheet with these columns in row 1: **Client, Email, Description, Quantity, Unit Price, Due Days, Status, Invoice Number, Pay Link**.\n4. In **New or updated row**, **Mark row sent** and **Mark row failed**, connect your Google account and pick the same spreadsheet and sheet.\n5. Add a test row with your own email address, set Status to `ready`, and run the workflow once with **Test workflow**. Then activate it.",
        "height": 440,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "e23e5a10-7741-41b1-a443-d5db433f6bfb",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -580,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Customize\n- Set the guard in **Ready rows only** to accept only `ready`, so half-typed rows are never invoiced.\n- Add more line-item columns (for example Tax Rate or Unit) and map them in **Create invoice**.\n- Pick a currency or invoice design in **Create invoice → Additional Fields** (node form) or the JSON body (HTTP form).\n- Change the email subject and message in **Send invoice**.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "4402a70a-7261-4fdd-a74b-7d26a6e2e795",
      "name": "Customize",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -580,
        180
      ]
    }
